  "staleness": "These populations are from the 2011 census, the last one India completed. The 2021 census was postponed and has not been held, so every per-capita figure computed from this divides a current count by a fifteen-year-old denominator. The error is not uniform: the states that have grown fastest since are the most overstated by it. Any rate built on this must print the denominator's year on the same line.",
